title: Quotes
---
body:

Lines I keep coming back to. Source noted where known, added as I find them, no particular order.

> "It's not about “educated” vs. “uneducated.” It's about “likes to read” and “doesn't like to read.”"
> — [Naval Ravikant](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Naval_Ravikant)

> "Read books are far less valuable than unread ones."
> — [Nassim Taleb](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nassim_Nicholas_Taleb)

> "Not everything that counts can be counted, and not everything that can be counted counts."
> — [Albert Einstein](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Albert_Einstein)

> "A good decision is based on knowledge and not on numbers."
> — [Plato](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plato)

there is no place in the world for ugly mathematics